# Audited non-grandchild fork() sites excluded from the grandchild-fork gate.
#
# Format: file:line:hash  # rationale
#   file    = repo-relative path
#   line    = line number as reported by the scanner (child-branch line for
#             recognised if(pid==0)/if(!pid) forms; fork() call line for
#             UNPARSED sites)
#   hash    = first 8 hex chars of sha256 of the trimmed line content
#
# Keying on file:line:hash rather than plain file:line means that both the
# line number AND the site content must match.  Updating a line number in
# the allowlist without re-auditing (bulk-renumber) fails on hash mismatch.
#
# A new fork() call added anywhere else in one of these files is still caught.
fds/scratch_block.c:123:22958d17        # exec-helper: fork/execlp to run mkfs.ext4; child execs immediately, no grandchild context
health/kmsg-monitor.c:435:cf01f487      # infrastructure daemon: forked once at early init before the child fleet exists; not a grandchild producer
utils/pc_format.c:230:22958d17          # exec-helper: fork/execlp for addr2line; child execs, no child branch reachable
utils/self_cgroup_fork.c:74:f3c50ad0    # produces first-generation child, not a grandchild; UNPARSED -- no if(pid==0) branch, child path returns to caller
